Package: attack-surface
Version: 0.23.0
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: python3, python3-requests, python3-dnspython, python3-yaml, nmap
Recommends: openssl
Suggests: wapiti, nikto, hydra, crackmapexec, bloodhound, metasploit-framework, sliver
Maintainer: Mahdi Khaligh <khalighmahdi@users.noreply.github.com>
Description: Modular attack-surface reconnaissance, blue-team monitoring & red team orchestration
 Discovers and grades the external attack surface of a domain:
 subdomain discovery, nmap -sV service banners, security-header auditing,
 technology fingerprinting, CDN/origin detection, admin-panel discovery,
 exposed CMS setup pages, subdomain-takeover fingerprints, baseline
 diffing for continuous monitoring, CPE-exact CVE watchlists (NVD) and
 safe active checks (TLS audit, login liveness, DNS AXFR/DNSSEC).
 Advanced modules: Cloud asset discovery (AWS/Azure/GCP), API security
 (OpenAPI/GraphQL/REST + fuzzing), SBOM supply chain analysis, MITRE
 ATT&CK mapping with Navigator layers, Executive/Technical/Compliance
 reporting (NIST/ISO27001/PCI-DSS/SOC2/GDPR), Jira/GitHub/SIEM/ChatOps
 integrations with RBAC. Red Team orchestration: Credential attacks
 (Hydra, Impacket, CrackMapExec), Metasploit RPC, AD/Entra ID attacks
 (BloodHound, Kerberoasting, DCSync), Lateral movement, Cloud exploitation,
 C2 management (Sliver), Post-exploitation, Persistence. Action Center
 with operator-gated execution and full audit logging. Exports XSS-safe
 HTML, CSV, Markdown, JSON; streams CEF syslog, Slack and Telegram alerts.
 Home-page: https://github.com/khalighmahdi/attack-surface
Tag: role::program, security::recon, implemented-in::python, interface::commandline
